s 1)} \\\\\n7^5 & = 16807 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 7)} \\\\\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nWe can see that the units digits repeat every 4 numbers: 7, 9, 3, 1. Therefore, to find the units digit of \\(7^{13}\\), we need to determine the position of 13 in the repeating cycle. We do this by finding the remainder when 13 is divided by 4:\n\\[\n13 \\div 4 = 3 \\text{ remainder } 1\n\\]\nThis means that \\(7^{13}\\) has the same units digit as \\(7^1\\), which is 7. So, the units digit of \\(17^{13}\\) is 7.\n\nNext, we need to find the units digit of \\(17^{13} - 17\\). Since the units digit of \\(17^{13}\\) is 7 and the units digit of 17 is 7, we subtract these units digits:\n\\[\n7 - 7 = 0\n\\]\nTherefore, the units digit of \\(17^{13} - 17\\) is \\(\\boxed{0}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{0}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:416"}
